# Emacs-like keymap for text editor LE.
# Abel Morabito <amorabito@funescoop.com.ar>
#
# Respelled for Braam, the way share/keymap was: a terminfo capability named an
# escape sequence and there are none here, so ${Left} and ${S-F3} name the keys.
# Upstream gave a modified key several spellings -- terminfo's and two of
# xterm's -- and only one resolved on a given terminal; here they are one name,
# so the duplicates are gone and so are the collisions they hid. The keys with
# no name here went with them: $kund, $kext, $kcan, $kspd, $krfr, $kel, $kdl.
#
# ^X is a prefix in this map, so ^X ^C quits and ^G cancels; ${Esc} is bound
# because ESC is a key here rather than the Alt prefix it was upstream.
